<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin signs double taxation treaties.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin signs double taxation treaties.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Boris Yeltsin signed a series of laws on Wednesday ratifying double taxation treaties with several countries, the presidential press service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The treaties are with the Czech Republic, Croatia, Philippines, Slovenia, China, Denmark, Slovakia, Albania, Canada, Mongolia, Yugoslavia and Switzerland.</p>
<p>Double taxation treaties enable non-residents to invest effectively net of tax in Russian government securities, of which new issues have been subject to a 15 percent tax on profits since early this month.</p>
<p>As a result foreign investors have been heavy buyers of recent issues of Treasury bills, narrowing the yield differential between taxable and older non-taxable issues.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
